    {
      "title": "Callbacks and the Error-First Convention",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Callbacks and the Error-First Convention",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Definition and signature",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Callback== = function passed to an async API",
                "The event loop calls it **later**, never inline in the caller's stack",
                "Error-first: `cb(err, result)`",
                "`err` is {green:null or undefined} on success"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Callbacks vs promises",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Callback",
                "Promise"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Return or await",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Nesting",
                  "**callback hell**",
                  "flat chain"
                ],
                [
                  "Errors",
                  "`cb(err)`",
                  "`.catch`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: readFile",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Check `err` first and ==return==",
                "`util.promisify` wraps this style into a promise"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "function read(path, cb) {",
                "  fs.readFile(path, 'utf8', (err, data) => {",
                "    if (err) return cb(err);",
                "    cb(null, data);",
                "  });",
                "}",
                "const readP = util.promisify(read);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why never throw in an async callback?** The try/catch has already exited; pass `cb(err)`.",
                "**What does promisify require?** An error-first `(err, value)` callback as the last argument.",
                "**Double-callback bug?** A missing `return` calls `cb` twice."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`if (err) return cb(err)` - the ==return== stops the second call."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Promises and async/await",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Promises and async/await",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Promise basics",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Pending==, then {green:fulfilled} or {red:rejected}, exactly once",
                "`.then` handles success, `.catch` rejection, `.finally` always runs",
                "`async` functions always return a ==promise==",
                "`await` pauses ==only that function==; a rejection becomes a throw for try/catch"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Combinators",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Settles"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Promise.all`",
                  "Rejects fast on first failure"
                ],
                [
                  "`allSettled`",
                  "Waits for all, reports each outcome"
                ],
                [
                  "`race`",
                  "First to settle, either way"
                ],
                [
                  "`any`",
                  "First success"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Awaits in a row run ==sequentially==; `Promise.all` runs them in ==parallel=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "const [a, b] = await Promise.all([getA(), getB()]) // parallel",
                "await getA(); await getB() // sequential"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Forgetting `await`: the promise is silently dropped",
                "`await` inside `forEach` does not wait; use `for...of` or `Promise.all` with `map`",
                "`return p` inside `try` without `await`: the catch is skipped"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Does await block the event loop?** No, only its own function pauses",
                "**Run tasks in parallel?** Start them all, then `Promise.all`",
                "**all vs allSettled?** Fail fast vs wait and report every outcome"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Express Error Middleware",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Express Error Middleware",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Definition and Mechanism",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Error handler has ==4 params==: `(err, req, res, next)`",
                "Found by ==arity==: keep `next` even if unused",
                "`next(err)` or a sync `throw` skips to it",
                "Register it ==last==, after routes and `app.use`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Express 4 vs 5",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Express 4",
                "Express 5"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Async rejection",
                  "Never reaches `next`: request {red:hangs}, Node 15+ may crash",
                  "{green:Forwarded} automatically"
                ],
                [
                  "Fix",
                  "Wrap, or catch-to-next helper",
                  "None needed"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`AppError` carries an ==HTTP status==; the handler maps it to the response"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "class AppError extends Error {",
                "  constructor(status, msg) { super(msg); this.status = status }",
                "}",
                "app.use((err, req, res, next) => {",
                "  res.status(err.status || 500).json({ error: err.message })",
                "})"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Double response: check `res.headersSent`, then `next(err)`",
                "Stack traces leaked in production",
                "Missing 404 handler before the error handler: unmatched routes skip your JSON format"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**How are handlers identified?** Four params (arity)",
                "**Why does Express 4 async hang?** The rejection never reaches `next(err)`",
                "**Where does it go?** After all routes and `app.use`"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Unhandled Rejections and Uncaught Exceptions",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Unhandled Rejections and Uncaught Exceptions",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Fires",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==unhandledRejection== fires when a promise rejects with no handler attached",
                "Node 15+: default is {red:crash} with a non-zero exit"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Last-Resort Hooks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Event",
                "Callback arg",
                "Do"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`unhandledRejection`",
                  "`reason`",
                  "log, exit"
                ],
                [
                  "`uncaughtException`",
                  "`err`",
                  "log, exit"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Hooks are for ==logging==, not recovery",
                "After uncaughtException the state is {red:unknown}",
                "Never keep serving as if nothing happened"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Log, Exit, Restart",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "process.on('unhandledRejection', (r) => {",
                "  logger.error(r);",
                "  process.exit(1);",
                "});"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Error",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Log",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "exit(1)",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Supervisor",
                    "sub": "PM2, Docker, Kubernetes",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Handle it earlier",
              "text": "Catch errors with `try/catch`, `.catch` and `next(err)`. The hooks are the net."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Node 15 change?** Unhandled rejections now crash the process",
                "**Unsafe after uncaughtException?** State is unknown",
                "**Where to handle errors?** At the source: try/catch, .catch, next(err)"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Environment Config and Graceful Shutdown",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Environment Config and Graceful Shutdown",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Env Config",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`process.env` holds ==strings only==",
                "Local: `.env` via dotenv or `--env-file`; **never commit** it",
                "Real values are set in the platform",
                "==Fail fast== at boot on missing vars",
                "Convert types: `Number(process.env.PORT)`",
                "Defaults only for non-secrets"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Shutdown on SIGTERM",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "SIGTERM / SIGINT",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "server.close()",
                    "sub": "no new connections",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Drain",
                    "sub": "in-flight requests",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Close DB, queues",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "exit(0)",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "process.on('SIGTERM', () => {",
                "  server.close(async () => {",
                "    await db.end()",
                "    process.exit(0)",
                "  })",
                "  setTimeout(() => process.exit(1), 10000).unref()",
                "})"
              ],
              "note": "forced exit after 10 s"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Ignoring SIGTERM in containers: killed after the grace period",
                "Keep-alive connections hold `server.close` open",
                "Exiting before cleanup finishes"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why SIGTERM, not SIGKILL?** SIGTERM can be caught to clean up; SIGKILL cannot",
                "**Why a forced-exit timeout?** Hung connections would block exit forever",
                "**Why validate env at boot?** Fail at deploy, not on the first request"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
