    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "What logs first, and why? `items.forEach(async id => await save(id)); console.log('done')`",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`done` logs first: forEach ignores the promises its callbacks return",
                "Fix: `for...of` with await, or `await Promise.all(items.map(save))`"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`Promise.all([a(), bFails(), c()])`: what happens, and what would allSettled give instead?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "all rejects at once with b's error, and the results of a and c are lost",
                "allSettled never rejects: it reports all three outcomes"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "In Express 4, an async handler throws. Why doesn't the error middleware run?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Express 4 ignores the rejected promise the handler returns",
                "The rejection goes unhandled, which crashes Node 15+ by default",
                "Fix: catch and call `next(err)`, or wrap the handler; Express 5 forwards it"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
